        "reason-1": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "category": "THE 3PM DIP",
            "title": "The 3pm dip isn’t a willpower problem",
            "content": "<p>You’re not lazy at 3pm. You’re three hours past lunch, running a body that has to turn what you ate into usable energy. That conversion runs on cofactors — B vitamins first among them. Pushing through doesn’t supply any. Neither does a fourth coffee.</p>"
          }
        },
        "reason-2": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "category": "CAFFEINE",
            "title": "The tiredness doesn’t go away. It waits.",
            "content": "<p>Caffeine adds nothing to your system. It blocks the signal that tells you you’re tired — the tiredness itself is still there, waiting. When the caffeine clears, the signal comes back with everything that piled up behind it. That’s the dip you keep answering with another cup, which is why it keeps coming back.</p>"
          }
        },
        "reason-3": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "category": "B COMPLEX",
            "title": "A complete B complex, in the forms your body uses directly",
            "content": "<p>B vitamins are the cofactors your metabolism draws on to convert food into energy. GOMU carries the full complex, including methylcobalamin and L-5-MTHF — the active forms, rather than the cheap ones your body has to convert first. A contribution to normal energy metabolism. Not a stimulant.</p>"
          }
        },
        "reason-4": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "category": "ADAPTOGENS",
            "title": "Some of that tiredness is load, not sleep",
            "content": "<p>Ashwagandha KSM-66 and rhodiola are adaptogens — plants traditionally used through demanding periods, mentally and physically, and included here at clinically documented doses. They won’t fix a schedule that doesn’t work. But a nervous system running hot from 9am is a real part of what 3pm feels like, and it isn’t a caffeine problem.</p>"
          }
        },
        "reason-5": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "category": "SUGAR",
            "title": "About 2g of sugar. Not a spike.",
            "content": "<p>A pastry or an energy drink at 3pm buys you a fast rise and a faster fall — you’ve felt both. A GOMU pack carries about 2g of sugar, the minimum the gummy format requires, with no artificial sweeteners. It isn’t built to spike you, so there’s nothing to come down from.</p>"
          }
        },
        "reason-6": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "category": "ONE PACK",
            "title": "One pack instead of a shelf of jars",
            "content": "<p>Energy in one bottle, B complex in another, magnesium in a third, adaptogens in a fourth — and by week two you take none of them. GOMU is 15–20 actives in a single daily pack: 8 gummies, 30 seconds, no water, 28 packs per pouch. The routine you keep beats the routine you optimise.</p>"
          }
        }
